From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Utkarsh Dalal <utkarsh.dalal@toptal.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:45:04 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] CodeMap: record indirect jump and call targets

With CodeMapIndirectBranches, an indirect jump or call whose target misses
the thread's L1 lookup cache leaves its guest RIP in the frame; the
dispatcher checks it against a per-thread table of seen pairs and, for a
new pair, appends a {site, target} record (marker 0xffffffdd, 36 bytes)
to the code map. Returns are not recorded. Nothing changes on the L1 hit
path or with the option off.

CodeMapIndirectResampleMS drops a slice of each thread's L1 at that
interval (an eighth of it in the first two minutes) so pairs whose target
was already cached are seen as well.

ParseCodeMap skips the new record.
